From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=96zcan=20O=C4=9Fuz?= <ozcan@oyd.org.tr>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:03:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Berrak: name, art and wording in place of Mozilla's marks

- klar flavour: app name "Berrak"; Berrak's launcher (adaptive-icon
  drawables, which is all minSdk 26 uses), notification, splash, onboarding,
  wordmark and search-widget art, copied onto the names and resource
  qualifiers upstream uses so they override main/.
- Debug builds lose Firefox's debug launcher and use the flavour's icon.
  klarBeta's onboarding logo and klarNightly's art go too (the latter sat
  outside res/ and was never packaged).
- tools/berrak/rebrand_strings.py rewrites the English strings that claim
  Mozilla authorship, Mozilla terms or Mozilla data collection, and deletes
  their translations so every locale falls back to the accurate English.
  It is idempotent and fails when upstream renames a key; rerun it after
  each rebase. Onboarding now names the MPL 2.0 and Berrak's privacy notice.

